\section{Connecting}\label{sec:fovconnect}

This chunk completes [[SessionConfigView]] (Chapter~\ref{ch:classic}). A tap on the button
resumes a paused session, asks before disconnecting a connected one, and otherwise connects.

Connecting first builds the endpoint. On visionOS it then hands the session the two immersive
space actions through [[immersivePresentationBehaviors]]: with [[.automatic]], the session opens
its immersive space when streaming starts, dismisses it when the session pauses or disconnects,
and presents it again on resume. This is the main behavioral difference from CloudXRKit, where
the application opens its immersive space after connecting. Letting the session do it keeps the
space in step with the stream, including transitions the application does not initiate, such as a
server closing the session; correspondingly, the launch view and the window manager open and
dismiss the classic space only (Chapter~\ref{ch:visionos}).

Hand tracking is an input capability the session must request. The capability type was added in
visionOS 27, so the request is made only there, after asking the user for authorization. Then the
session connects; any error, thrown by the endpoint validation or by the framework, is logged and
shown under the form.

<<foveated connect flow>>=
#if FOVEATED_STREAMING
    private func handleFoveatedConnectButtonTap() {
        let session = appModel.foveatedSession

        switch session.status {
        case .paused:
            Task { @MainActor in
                do {
                    try await session.resume()
                    completionHandler()
                } catch {
                    Self.logger.error("Foveated streaming resume failed: \(error.localizedDescription)")
                    appModel.foveatedConnectError = error.localizedDescription
                }
            }
        case .connected:
            appModel.showDisconnectionAlert = true
        default:
            doConnectFoveated()
        }
    }

    private func doConnectFoveated() {
        let session = appModel.foveatedSession
        appModel.foveatedConnectError = nil

        Task { @MainActor in
            do {
                let endpoint = try foveatedEndpointKind.endpoint(
                    hostAddress: hostAddress,
                    port: foveatedPort,
                    serverName: remoteServerName
                )

#if os(visionOS)
                // The session opens the immersive space once streaming starts and dismisses it
                // on disconnect, so neither LaunchView nor WindowStateManager opens it.
                session.immersivePresentationBehaviors = .automatic(openImmersiveSpace, dismissImmersiveSpace)

                if #available(visionOS 27.0, *) {
                    let capabilities: Set<FoveatedStreamingSession.InputCapability> = enableHandTracking ? [.handTracking] : []
                    if !capabilities.isEmpty {
                        _ = await session.requestAuthorization(for: capabilities)
                    }
                    session.requestedInputCapabilities = capabilities
                }
#endif

                try await session.connect(endpoint: endpoint)
                completionHandler()
            } catch {
                Self.logger.error("Foveated streaming connection failed: \(error.localizedDescription)")
                appModel.foveatedConnectError = error.localizedDescription
            }
        }
    }
#endif
@
\section{Build configuration}\label{sec:condition}

Neither library ships for the simulator: the visionOS simulator SDK has no FoveatedStreaming
framework, and Apple's xcframework has only a device slice. The fork keeps NVIDIA's ability to run
the classic backend in the visionOS simulator by compiling the foveated code only for device SDKs.
The condition [[FOVEATED_STREAMING]] is set with SDK-conditional build settings in
[[Config.xcconfig]], which all targets use as their base configuration; the [[$(inherited)]]
keeps the [[DEBUG]] condition the targets set themselves. The iOS target cannot be built for the
iOS simulator at all, because the StreamingSession package is linked unconditionally; NVIDIA's
iOS client needs ARKit's spatial tracking, which the simulator lacks anyway.

The file also sets the version, now 6.1.0, and the bundle identifier.

<<Config.xcconfig>>=
//
//  Config.xcconfig
//  CloudXR Viewer
//

// Configuration settings file format documentation can be found at:
// https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcode/adding-a-build-configuration-file-to-your-project

// Build configuration
MARKETING_VERSION = 6.1.0
PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.nvidia.cloudxr-viewer

// Apple's FoveatedStreaming framework (visionOS) and StreamingSession package (iOS) ship for
// devices only, so the foveated backend is compiled into device builds only.
SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS[sdk=xros*] = $(inherited) FOVEATED_STREAMING
SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS[sdk=iphoneos*] = $(inherited) FOVEATED_STREAMING
@
\section{Entitlements and property lists}

The visionOS target's entitlements add [[com.apple.developer.foveated-streaming-session]] to the
low-latency streaming entitlement NVIDIA already used. Both are granted to members of the Apple
Developer Program.



<<CloudXRViewer/visionOS/CloudXRViewer-visionOS.entitlements>>=
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.foveated-streaming-session</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.low-latency-streaming</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
@
System discovery browses for the Bonjour service type of Apple's session protocol. An
application that browses the local network must declare the types it uses in
[[NSBonjourServices]], so both property lists name [[_apple-foveated-streaming._tcp]]. The
remaining keys are NVIDIA's: usage descriptions for hand tracking and world sensing, file sharing,
and two application identifiers filled in from build settings.

The visionOS property list:

<<CloudXRViewer/visionOS/CloudXRViewer-visionOS-Info.plist>>=
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSBonjourServices</key>
	<array>
		<string>_apple-foveated-streaming._tcp</string>
	</array>
	<key>NSHandsTrackingUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Enables sending hand positions to a server.</string>
	<key>NSWorldSensingUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Enables placing objects.</string>
	<key>UIFileSharingEnabled</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NISSAN_CONFIGURATOR_APP_ID</key>
	<string>$(NISSAN_CONFIGURATOR_APP_ID)</string>
	<key>PURSE_CONFIGURATOR_APP_ID</key>
	<string>$(PURSE_CONFIGURATOR_APP_ID)</string>
</dict>
</plist>
@
